  "storyboard": {
    "greet": "Ana asks Luis how he is and he answers. Then Ana and Sofía discuss a clearly indicated girl: she always refers to that same girl. The two adults are the questioner and respondent; the girl is not made to describe herself as she.",
    "rest": "Ana asks Sofía about the established grandfather after his walk. Both look toward the same grandfather; Sofía answers about him, with a matched closer answer view.",
    "food": "Ana asks the baby’s parent how the baby is. The parent answers; the baby never speaks the third-person line. A subsequent food request has its own customer, server, handover and receipt.",
    "water": "Luis is thirsty after the walk. He requests water from that server, receives it and thanks them. Keep cup ownership consistent."
  },
